# Clean Code

Source: [clean-code.mdc](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules)

## Names & constants
- Replace magic numbers with named constants (risk thresholds 50/80, latency SLO 50ms)
- Names reveal intent: `evaluate_event`, `severity_counts`, not `process2`

## Functions
- Single responsibility; extract when a function needs a comment to explain its purpose
- Early returns and guard clauses over deep nesting

## DRY & structure
- One source of truth for API types (`lib/types.ts` ↔ Pydantic models)
- Related code stays together: detector + test, route + integration test

## Comments
- Explain *why*, not *what*; document non-obvious security or latency constraints

## Refactoring
- Leave touched files cleaner; don't drive-by refactor unrelated modules
- Fix technical debt only when it blocks the current task

## Tests
- Bug fixes include a regression test when feasible
- Test edge cases: empty ingest batch, missing campaign data, WebSocket disconnect
